#: ../../src/regionorderhelp.cpp:36
msgid ""
"Custom rule syntax\n"
"\n"
"Patterns separated by commas or semicolons. A region name is compared "
"against them in order, and the first one it matches decides its group; "
"earlier groups come first, and names inside a group keep their natural "
"order.\n"
"\n"
"* matches any run of characters, ? matches exactly one. Matching is case-"
"sensitive and uses the region name without the file extension. Names that "
"match no pattern follow the matched ones in natural order, so no region is "
"lost. An empty rule falls back to natural order.\n"
"\n"
"Example: with 2*, 1* the regions 2b, 1a, 10c come out as 2b, 1a, 10c; with "
"part* all part names come first."
msgstr ""

